      "writtenOn": "2022-08-29T16:43:08Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "\u003e  cross checked to see if \"PE_FLAGS_VDM_SETUP_DONE\" is set in drs_swap_run function after DRS swap rejection. But couldn\u0027t see it set.\n\nUnder ordinary circumstances, we set this flag when we complete the mode entry process or when one of the discovery/mode entry steps fails. In this case, discovery \"fails\" before it even starts. To cover this case, we could equivalently set the flag in `pe_drs_send_swap_run`, but I think the code is easier to follow when we set the flag near the rest of the discovery code.\n\n\u003e 2. Shouldn\u0027t we consider the DR_SWAP rejection condition when we hotplug the charger?\n\nThe UFP/PD 2.0 check in `pe_attempt_port_discovery` covers the DR Swap reject condition. We won\u0027t enter `pe_attempt_port_discovery` until we\u0027ve already tried to become DFP, so if we aren\u0027t, that must mean the DR Swap was rejected.",
      "parentUuid": "9abcf6a9_d8e8524a",
